## Verdict

Revise before implementation. One MCP server and shared services are sound, but the plan leaves charge recovery, concurrent writes and authorization behavior underspecified. Section 4b promises ATS reliability and export fidelity that the proposed renderer and verification cannot yet establish. This was a read-only review; no files changed and no application checks ran.

## Findings

1. { finding: "Credit idempotency is not job idempotency. Captured reservation keys return RESERVATION_SPENT rather than replaying results. generation_status cannot distinguish concurrent operations or fence a redelivered consumer. The fit discount also requires a server-owned continuation claim.", severity: "high", evidence: src/db/repos/credits.ts:1239; src/app/api/agent-v2/route.ts:875; PLAN §3, fix: "Persist operations keyed by owner, operation key and input hash, with result, reservation, lease and attempt/version. Return the existing operation on retry. Preserve fit-continuation eligibility. Add enqueue reconciliation, per-message acknowledgment, DLQ recovery and cancellation fencing." }

2. { finding: "The existing refund machinery explicitly admits losing refunds after a crash. Queue retries don't repair a reservation already marked released or partially refunded before credits were restored.", severity: "high", evidence: src/db/repos/credits.ts:1420, src/db/repos/credits.ts:1472, fix: "Make reservation transition, credit restoration and ledger entry atomic using D1 batch operations, or persist individually idempotent refund obligations and reconcile them. Test termination between every transition and credit write." }

3. { finding: "Adding persistKit doesn't create one write path. An already-open browser still submits entire stale documents, fit data, template and generation status after unrelated local changes, overwriting MCP results.", severity: "high", evidence: src/hooks/useSupabaseSync.ts:648; src/db/repos/sessions.ts:126, fix: "Remove browser ownership of generated fields. Use explicit edit services with expected revisions and conditional updates. Refresh/invalidate browser state after external mutations. Test an open stale tab against generation, rewrites and template changes." }

4. { finding: "Several reusable chat tools don't persist their advertised mutations. set_cv_template returns a client effect; CV edits return an object for the browser to apply. Their outline gate is request-local, incompatible with separate stateless MCP calls.", severity: "high", evidence: src/lib/agents/chat-tools/app-tools.ts:69; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/cv-tools.ts:119; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/types.ts:99, fix: "Extract mutation services that load owned state and persist conditionally. Expose revision-bound outline handles, or resolve validated edits atomically inside each tool. Don't reuse client-effect handlers as completed MCP operations." }

5. { finding: "JWT verification alone doesn't implement Connected apps revocation, and advertising read/write scopes doesn't enforce individual tools. The callback allowlist also contradicts 'every other MCP client' support.", severity: "high", evidence: PLAN §1, §3; [Better Auth MCP](https://better-auth.com/docs/plugins/mcp), fix: "Pass verified claims into each request's tool context; enforce a tool-to-scope map. Define access-token revocation semantics, refresh rotation and queued-work policy after revocation/account deletion. Validate exact registered callbacks, PKCE and resource binding; bound CIMD fetching and registration abuse. Test read-only tokens against every write." }

6. { finding: "Reading CV facts from D1 doesn't prevent an injected JD/tool result from inducing save_cv, deletion, overwrite or repeated paid calls. Existing chat handlers rely on user-message gates and human confirmation chips that external clients don't inherit.", severity: "high", evidence: src/lib/agents/chat-tools/kit-tools.ts:1; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/cv-tools.ts:28; PLAN §3, §7, fix: "Keep untrusted content distinct from instructions and remove behavioral directives from tool results. Define confirmation for destructive replacements and authorized spending limits across all clients. Add concurrent-job limits and shared web/MCP budgets, including free parsing, screening and exports. Test hostile JDs across multiple turns." }

7. { finding: "The print token doesn't authorize protected photo subrequests: /api/files still requires a session cookie. Token transport, atomic single-use enforcement and signed-download authorization are unspecified. Content/template-only cache keys omit rendering options and versioning.", severity: "high", evidence: src/app/api/files/[...key]/route.ts:19; src/storage/paths.ts:59; PLAN §4a, fix: "Prefer passing server-rendered HTML with embedded owned photos to Browser Run. Otherwise bind render grants to owner, document revision and purpose; use atomic consumption, no-store, no-referrer and token-log redaction. Sign exact export objects with expiry. Authorize cache hits and include photo bytes, locale, paper, format, fonts and renderer version. Purge exports on deletion." }

8. { finding: "DOM order and tagging cannot guarantee that ATS parsers read two columns without interleaving. GermanATSTemplate currently places skills/certifications before experience in DOM order, contrary to §4b's stated sequence.", severity: "high", evidence: src/components/cv-templates/GermanATSTemplate.tsx:230, :335, :367; [Greenhouse parsing limitations](https://support.greenhouse.io/hc/en-us/articles/200989175-Unsuccessful-resume-parse), fix: "Distinguish visual-template support from demonstrated parser compatibility. Offer a single-column ATS default in both markets, retain all six visual choices and measure each. Don't advertise universal ATS reliability or silently reorder user-edited content." }

9. { finding: "Browser Run's simple PDF call doesn't establish font readiness, image completion, tagging quality, language or Author metadata. Puppeteer's tagged output is experimental. Existing full-sheet widths plus PDF margins can shrink or overflow content; 'never split an entry' is impossible when an entry exceeds one page.", severity: "high", evidence: PLAN §4a–4b; src/components/cv-templates/GermanATSTemplate.tsx:47; [PDF options](https://pptr.dev/api/puppeteer.pdfoptions), fix: "Spike the deployed Browser Run output first. Specify paper, scale, background and one margin owner; wait for verified fonts and decoded images. Validate structure-tree order, Unicode maps and metadata after any postprocessing. Define controlled continuation for oversized entries, widow/orphan rules and readable minimum type sizes." }

10. { finding: "Reusing current templates silently drops source skills. Every template caps items per group at five; four also cap groups. Matching the canvas can therefore reproduce incomplete exports.", severity: "high", evidence: src/lib/cv-structure/render-caps.ts:8; src/components/cv-templates/USPremiumATSTemplate.tsx:278, :350, fix: "Remove silent truncation from the shared renderer or explicitly model user-approved exclusions. Assert every intended skill, bullet, project and custom section survives PDF and DOCX export, including fixtures beyond all current caps." }

11. { finding: "The cover-letter 'body' is already a complete letter, not merely prose. Wrapping it with another sender, greeting and closing duplicates content. The current prompt also expressly forbids company-address lines.", severity: "high", evidence: src/lib/agents/prompts/cover-letter-prompt.ts:205, :217, :235; src/lib/utils/cover-letter-export.ts:10, fix: "Introduce a structured letter contract separating addresses, date, subject, salutation, paragraphs and closing. Define a legacy-letter migration path. Use verified recipient details, allow unknown addresses and never invent them to fill DIN fields." }

12. { finding: "The ATS proxy cannot run as specified: OpenResume's documented parser consumes PDFs through PDF.js, not DOCX. It isn't independent evidence for German extraction or commercial ATS compatibility. Heading/title checks also miss lost bullets and incorrect date-to-employer associations.", severity: "high", evidence: PLAN §4b; [OpenResume parser](https://github.com/xitanggg/open-resume), fix: "Pin parser versions and fixtures. Add independent DOCX XML/content checks and Word/LibreOffice rendering checks. Compare complete text and field associations, test German headings and enforce file-size budgets, including Greenhouse's 2.5 MB limit. Test overflow, failed fonts/photos and actual deployed Browser Run output." }

13. { finding: "Annotations understate destructive effects: regeneration overwrites documents, template/status/profile updates replace state and credit spending is consequential. The plan also omits explicit boolean annotations for every tool. Copying existing descriptions/results would import instructions such as 'Tell the user' and billing navigation.", severity: "high", evidence: PLAN §4; src/lib/agents/chat-tools/kit-tools.ts:84; [OpenAI annotation requirements](https://developers.openai.com/plugins/plugin-guidelines), fix: "Set all three booleans per tool and audit actual effects. Mark overwrites appropriately; split operations with materially different effects. Return factual data and neutral entitlement errors. Review every exposed description and failure response against both directories." }

14. { finding: "Delivery dependencies and review classifications are wrong. PR 4 depends on PR 2 despite the parallel-start instruction. PR 5 depends only on PR 3 despite promising exports. Signed links and private render routes fall under the sensitive review row.", severity: "high", evidence: PLAN §5; AGENTS.md security review rules, fix: "Parallelize an isolated rendering spike, then integrate exports after persistence. Make distribution depend on completed exports and all-client acceptance. Give export authorization sensitive review. Keep incomplete production tools disabled, not merely unlisted." }

15. { finding: "DIN 5008 is described as a style sketch, not an implementable conformance specification. 'DIN-style margins' doesn't define a CV standard, and Germany isn't a universal EU hiring convention. Uploaded DOB/nationality isn't itself a request to publish them.", severity: "low", evidence: PLAN §4b; [DIN 5008 scope](https://www.dinmedia.de/de/norm/din-5008/318422674), fix: "Name the edition and chosen letter variant; specify measured address-field geometry, spacing and continuation rules. Form B's address field starts 45 mm from the top and measures 85 × 45 mm ([layout reference](https://c.wgr.de/d/25aef4740c0c03f859bd05b3db0a3c333bcf16cdf9baef604a1e104b803a5b35.pdf/978-3-8045-4780-3_28.pdf)). Treat page counts as guidance; make personal-data/photo inclusion explicit." }

16. { finding: "The claim that Browser Run lacks Arial and Georgia is false. Its documented installed fonts include both. Self-hosting alternatives also won't replace hardcoded font-family declarations automatically.", severity: "low", evidence: PLAN §4b; [supported fonts](https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/reference/supported-fonts/), fix: "Correct the rationale. If deterministic font files remain desired, bind them explicitly in shared templates, include required weights/glyph coverage and verify embedded PDF fonts plus DOCX substitution behavior." }

17. { finding: "The cost estimate mixes Browser Sessions concurrency charges into Quick Actions and overstates per-PDF browser cost.", severity: "low", evidence: PLAN §4a; [Browser Run pricing](https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/pricing/), fix: "Quick Actions charges browser hours only. Three seconds at $0.09/hour is $0.000075. Label $0 as incremental infrastructure cost and account separately for existing model usage, retries and shared allowances." }

## Missing from the plan

- Free draft creation, direct CV/letter/email edits, primary/master CV deletion and photo upload/removal. Humans already have these through `src/db/actions.ts:139`, `CVPanel.tsx:484`, `CoverLetterPanel.tsx:477` and `EmailPanel.tsx:274`.
- Career-profile/search-strategy operations, feed consent withdrawal and complete feed settings, including automation and timezone. Relevant routes exist under `src/app/api/job-feed/`.
- `get_cv_outline`, required by the proposed reused editing tools; language override; `.txt`, `.md` and `.tex` upload parity. Add `cv_docx` to §4a's export enum.
- Queue consumer wiring through OpenNext request context (`src/worker.ts:41`, `src/db/client.ts:29`). Specify ID-only messages, batching, concurrency and deadlines against the [128 KB message, 15-minute wall-time and default 30-second CPU limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/queues/platform/limits/).
- Negative E2E coverage: cross-user IDs, expired/replayed render grants, refresh/revocation, duplicate requests, Queue crashes, partial refunds and stale-tab writes. Use Playwright Test with trace/video.
- Retention/deletion rules and disclosures covering R2 exports, Browser Run and analytics; renewable reviewer credits and seeded fixtures. Anthropic requires testing every tool in Claude, not just one workflow ([submission checklist](https://claude.com/docs/connectors/building/submission)).

## DISMISSED

- One server for multiple clients: sound; packaging can remain client-specific.
- Stateless MCP and deprecated McpAgent: supported by [Cloudflare's current SDK documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-07-27-agents-sdk-v0.20.0-mcp-sdk-v2/).
- Better Auth MCP/CIMD direction: current and appropriate; durable OAuth records remain necessary.
- The 1.5-credit continuation price: correct in `src/lib/credit-costs.ts:3`; AGENTS.md's summary is stale.
- Existing paid-account access: allowed; excluding checkout tools is appropriate.
- Client components: `'use client'` alone doesn't prevent server prerendering, though GermanClassic currently imports settings behavior.
- html2canvas replacement: justified; today's CV export is rasterized.
- oklch: no demonstrated Chromium blocker; the existing workaround targets html2canvas.
- Queue generation: justified for disconnect survival; return an operation immediately by default instead of making every client wait 45 seconds.
